Read complete. I'll add a **full-size toggle** to the slide show header: when enabled the active slide occupies the whole slides area (100% × 100%), the neighbours animate out of view, and the toggle is also reachable via the `F` key or a double-click on the slide.

| Area | Change |
|---|---|
| **Header** | New toggle button (`fa-expand`/`fa-compress`, `aria-pressed`) next to *Close* |
| **Slide geometry** | `slideStyle()` returns 100% × 100% for the active slide and pushes neighbours off-screen with `opacity: 0` when `fullSize` is on |
| **Interaction** | `toggleFullSize()` + `F` key + `@dblclick` on the active slide |
| **Transition** | Same `transition-all duration-500 ease-out`, so fit ↔ full morphs smoothly |

