## Specifications

| Dimension | Fit mode (default) | Full size mode |
|---|---|---|
| Active slide | `width: 80%`, `height: 80%`, `scale(1)`, `rounded-xl` | `width: 100%`, `height: 100%`, `scale(1)`, `rounded-none` |
| Neighbour ±1 | `left ±32%`, `scale(0.6)`, `opacity 0.6`, `z-index 20` | `left ±60%`, `scale(0.8)`, `opacity 0`, `z-index 20` |
| Others | `left ±48%`, `scale(0.4)`, `opacity 0`, `z-index 10` | `left ±60%`, `scale(0.6)`, `opacity 0`, `z-index 10` |
| Header control | `btn btn-sm btn-ghost`, icon `fa-expand`, label **Full** | icon `fa-compress`, label **Fit**, `aria-pressed="true"` |
| Shortcuts | `←`/`→` navigate, `Esc` closes | `F` toggles, `double-click` on the slide toggles |

## Anti-patterns avoided

- ❌ Removing neighbours from the DOM in full size — they stay mounted and merely animate out, so toggling back has no reload flicker.
- ❌ A separate "expanded" layout branch — one `slideStyle()` computes both modes, so the transitions stay symmetric.
- ❌ Hiding the control behind a hover state — the toggle is a persistent, labeled button in the header (also reachable by `F` and double-click).

## Accessibility

- [x] Toggle is a real `<button>` with `title`, `aria-label` and `aria-pressed`
- [x] State is not conveyed by icon alone — the label switches between **Full** and **Fit**
- [x] Keyboard operable (`F`), and the key handler now ignores keystrokes typed in inputs/textareas
- [x] Thumbnails and carousel navigation unchanged — still buttons with `aria-label`, arrows still work
